    q: "My slush machine is running but the drink won't freeze. What's wrong?",
    a: "Two usual suspects. First, the refrigeration side: low charge from a slow leak, a condenser packed with bar dust, or a tired compressor that can't pull the bowl down. Second, the mix isn't turning against the cylinder wall the way it should, so nothing scrapes the ice off, and the machine just chills soupy product. Our techs check both. It also helps to know most slush needs 12 to 18 percent sugar (Brix) to freeze right, watered-down mix will never slush no matter how healthy the machine is. $120 commercial diagnostic, waived with the repair."
  },
  {
    q: "Product is leaking from behind the auger or under the bowl. Fixable?",
    a: "Yes, and it's one of the most common calls we get. The seal behind the auger or paddle is a wear part, it hardens and weeps sticky product down the front of the machine, and on gravity bowls a cracked or flattened bowl gasket does the same. We rebuild the front seal and gaskets, check the bearing and shaft for wear while we're in there, and sanitize. Left alone, a weeping seal lets product into the drive and turns a $200 seal job into a gearbox job."
  },
  {
    q: "The auger or paddle stopped turning and the machine is grinding.",
    a: "That's the drive. On belt-and-gearbox machines (Bunn, Taylor, Elmeco, Donper) it's usually the gear motor, gear reducer, or a stretched drive belt, and the grinding is worn gears. On Ugolini magnetic-transmission bowls there's no gearbox in the product path, so it's the drive motor or a slipping magnet coupling instead. We diagnose which and quote before we open a wallet."
  },
  {
    q: "Do you service Bunn, Taylor, Ugolini, Elmeco, FBD, and Donper?",
    a: "Yes, those are the machines we see most across LA. Bunn Ultra-2 and Ultra NX, Taylor two-, three-, and four-flavor frozen cocktail freezers, Ugolini MT and HT granita bowls, Elmeco Big Biz and First Class, FBD and Cornelius frozen carbonated dispensers, and Donper XC slush machines. We carry common seals, valves, and drive parts on the van for the popular models; specialty parts ship 2 to 7 days through distribution."
  },
  {
    q: "Do you fix margarita machines for events and rentals?",
    a: "We do. LA runs on event rental, and a frozen margarita machine that quits the morning of a Santa Monica wedding or a Hollywood party is an emergency. We service the rental-fleet machines (Donper, Taylor, and the Bunn/Island Oasis frozen cocktail units) for both venues and rental operators, and we can turn around a seal, drive, or refrigeration fix same-day in most of the LA basin."
  },
  {
    q: "What does slush machine repair cost?",
    a: "Diagnostic is $120 commercial tier, waived with the repair, no emergency surcharge. Typical work our techs quote across LA: front seal and gasket rebuild $180 to $320, mixing auger or spiral $200 to $420, gear motor or reducer $320 to $680, magnetic drive motor $280 to $560, dispense valve or spigot rebuild $120 to $260, condenser fan motor $260 to $460, refrigerant leak repair and recharge $500 to $1,100, control board $320 to $620, and compressor replacement $900 to $1,800. Same Day Appliance Repair, EPA 608 Universal certified for the sealed system."
  },
  {
    q: "Do you service frozen carbonated beverage (FCB) machines like FBD and Cornelius?",
    a: "We service the machine itself, the refrigeration, the barrel, the drive, the seals, and the dispense valves on FBD and Cornelius frozen carbonated units. The carbonation and syrup bag-in-box side (CO2 regulators, BIB pumps, water/syrup ratios) crosses into beverage-line trade, and for a pure syrup-system problem we'll tell you straight and refer it. Anything mechanical or refrigeration on the barrel is ours."
  }
];

