<!-- 01 INTRO -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">Frozen beverage service</p>
    <h2>A dead slush machine on a hot LA Saturday is lost revenue by the hour.</h2>

    <p>Commercial slush, slushie, margarita, and frozen beverage machine repair is a lane most appliance shops skip, and our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair run it every week, from the bars off Sunset and the cafés in Silver Lake to the c-store and cinema frozen-carbonated lines in Long Beach and the event-rental margarita fleets that feed weddings in Santa Monica and parties across Beverly Hills and Pasadena. These machines look simple and aren't: a refrigerated freezing cylinder, a mixing auger or paddle driven by a gearbox or a magnet, a front seal that lives in sugar all day, and on FCB units a carbonation loop on top. When one quits mid-service, the drink turns to soup and the register goes quiet. We cover LA, Orange, Ventura, Santa Barbara, San Bernardino, Riverside, and San Diego. $120 commercial diagnostic, waived with the repair, no emergency surcharge. EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410) for the sealed refrigeration side.</p>

    <p class="intro-speakable">When a bar manager in West Hollywood or an event-rental operator searches slush machine repair near me on a Friday afternoon, the clock is already running: soft product, a line at the bar, and a machine that won't pull down. Frozen beverage machines fail differently than ice machines. Different drive, different seals, different consistency problems, same sealed-refrigeration diagnostics underneath.</p>

    <p>Our techs service these across LA County, Orange County, Ventura, San Bernardino, and Riverside, with same-day dispatch into Downtown LA, Hollywood, West Hollywood, Beverly Hills, Santa Monica, Culver City, Long Beach, and Pasadena bars, cafés, restaurants, c-stores, and rental venues. Gravity granita and slush bowls (Ugolini, Elmeco, Bunn), frozen cocktail and margarita freezers (Taylor, Bunn, Donper), and frozen carbonated dispensers (FBD, Cornelius). Soft-serve and gelato are a separate machine and a separate page: see <a href="/commercial/ice-machines/soft-serve/">commercial soft-serve repair</a>.</p>

    <p>BHGS #A49573. BBB Accredited. Phones answered 24/7, because frozen drink machines fail on Friday night and Saturday afternoon, not Tuesday at 10 AM. Parent context: <a href="/commercial/ice-machines/">commercial ice machine repair</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 02 WHAT WE SERVICE -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-number">What we service</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Four kinds of frozen beverage machine.</h2>

    <h3 class="series-h3">Slush &amp; Granita (open bowl, gravity)</h3>
    <p>The clear polycarbonate bowls you see on a bar or café counter, one to three of them, with a paddle or auger turning inside. Ugolini MT (MT1, MT2, MT3, magnetic transmission) and HT granita, Elmeco Big Biz and First Class, and Bunn Ultra hoppers cover most of what we service. Common failures: the bowl won't freeze (refrigeration or the mix not turning), the paddle stops (drive), or product weeps from the front seal. See <a href="/commercial/ice-machines/">ice machine repair</a> for the ice side.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">Frozen Cocktail &amp; Margarita</h3>
    <p>Higher-volume freezing cylinders built for margaritas, daiquiris, piña coladas, and vodka slushes. Taylor two-, three-, and four-flavor frozen cocktail freezers (pressurized and non-pressurized), Bunn frozen cocktail units, and Donper XC machines. These live in bars and in the LA event-rental fleet. Failures cluster on the refrigeration, the gearbox, and consistency (too soft or too hard).</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">Frozen Carbonated Beverage (FCB)</h3>
    <p>The 7-Eleven Slurpee style dispensers in c-stores, cinemas, and quick-serve. FBD (562, 772) and Cornelius carbonated barrels. We service the barrel, the freezing cylinder, the auger and beater, the seals, and the dispense valves. The CO2 and syrup bag-in-box side is beverage-line trade; we're honest about where the line is.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">Frozen Drink &amp; Smoothie Dispensers</h3>
    <p>Non-carbonated frozen juice, lemonade, tea, and coffee dispensers, plus smoothie machines. Bunn Ultra-2 and Ultra NX with the reversing, torque-sensing auger are the workhorses here. Same drive, seal, and refrigeration playbook as the slush bowls.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 03 COMMON FAILURES -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">Common failures</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Where these machines actually break.</h2>

    <ol class="num-list">
      <li><strong>Won't freeze / soupy product.</strong> Refrigeration first: low charge from a slow leak, a condenser choked with bar dust and grease, or a compressor losing capacity. Then the mix: if the auger isn't scraping ice off the cylinder wall, nothing freezes evenly. We check charge and superheat, clean the condenser, and confirm the drive before quoting a compressor.</li>
      <li><strong>Front / barrel seal leaking.</strong> The seal behind the auger lives in sugar and hardens over time. It weeps product down the front, and on FCB and cocktail barrels it lets air in and messes consistency. A wear part, cheap to do on schedule, expensive to ignore because leaked product wrecks the drive.</li>
      <li><strong>Auger or paddle not turning.</strong> Gear motor, gear reducer, or drive belt on Bunn, Taylor, Elmeco, and Donper. On Ugolini magnetic-drive bowls there's no gearbox in the product path, so it's the motor or a slipping magnet coupling. Grinding usually means worn gears.</li>
      <li><strong>Scraper blades worn.</strong> The blades on the auger scrape ice off the freezing cylinder. Worn or warped blades leave an ice layer that insulates the wall, and the machine runs and runs without making good slush.</li>
      <li><strong>Dispense valve or spigot leaking / clogged.</strong> Sticky product dries in the valve. We rebuild the valve, replace the O-rings, and free the handle.</li>
      <li><strong>Refrigerant slow leak.</strong> Same EPA 608 rule as any sealed system: find the leak, repair it, evacuate, and recharge. We don't just top it off.</li>
      <li><strong>Control / thermostat fault.</strong> Consistency drifts, or the machine won't hold set temperature. Board or thermostat diagnostic, not always a full board replacement.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 04 BRANDS -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-number">Brands we service</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">The frozen beverage brands we see in LA.</h2>

    <h3 class="series-h3">Bunn</h3>
    <p>Ultra-2, Ultra-2 HP, and Ultra NX frozen beverage dispensers, the reversing, torque-sensing auger platform, plus Bunn's frozen cocktail units. Common in cafés, c-stores, and juice/lemonade programs. Ultra NX uses a redesigned auger-drive and seal for longer service life.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">Taylor</h3>
    <p>Two-, three-, and four-flavor frozen cocktail and frozen beverage freezers, pressurized and non-pressurized. High-volume bar and event equipment. Taylor's own service network flags refrigeration, gearbox, and consistency as the usual repair areas, which matches what we see in the field.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">Ugolini</h3>
    <p>Italian. MT series (MT1, MT2, MT3) granita and slush bowls built on Ugolini's magnetic transmission, plus the HT range and MiniGel. The magnetic drive means no gearbox seal in the product path, so drive repairs look different from belt-and-gearbox machines.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">Elmeco</h3>
    <p>Italian. Big Biz and First Class (FC Millennium) granita and slush dispensers, plus the newer BLarge line. Common in bars and event rental for margaritas and Italian granita.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">FBD &amp; Cornelius</h3>
    <p>Frozen carbonated beverage dispensers. FBD 562 and 772 multi-flavor barrels, and Cornelius (Marmon Foodservice) FCB units. The Slurpee-style machines in c-stores and cinemas. We handle the mechanical and refrigeration side; carbonation/syrup systems are beverage-line trade.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">Donper</h3>
    <p>Donper USA XC slush and margarita machines (XC112 single bowl, XC212 dual-bowl Mini Marg, XC336 triple 3.2-gallon). Budget-friendly and very common in the LA margarita rental fleet.</p>

    <p>We carry common seals, valves, scraper blades, and drive parts on the van for the popular models. Specialty parts ship 2 to 7 days through distribution. Bunn brand detail: <a href="/brands/bunn-slushie-machine-repair/">Bunn slushie machine repair</a>. Pricing reference: <a href="/price-list/commercial-slushie-machine-repair-cost/">commercial slushie machine repair cost</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 05 RECENT REPAIRS -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-number">Real repairs</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Composite stories from the route.</h2>

    <p class="lead">Frozen beverage jobs typical of what we see across LA. Names omitted; models, symptoms, and parts are representative.</p>

    <div class="story-grid">
      <div class="story-card">
        <h3>West Hollywood, Bunn Ultra-2 HP dual hopper, café/bar, 5 years old</h3>
        <p>One hopper making slush, the other running soupy no matter the setting. Tech dispatched from the West Hollywood branch. Diagnosed: worn auger drive on the soft side plus a hardened front seal weeping product into the drive housing. Rebuilt the front seal and gaskets, replaced the gear motor, cleaned the condenser (packed with dust behind the bar), and confirmed both hoppers pulling down and holding slush. Total: $120 plus $520 parts plus 2 hours = $860.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="story-card">
        <h3>Hollywood, Ugolini MT2 granita bowl, café, 6 years old</h3>
        <p>Left bowl warm, paddle not turning, right bowl fine. Because it's a magnetic-drive machine there's no gearbox to fail in the product path. Diagnosed: drive motor on the left position weak and a magnet coupling not engaging under load. Replaced the drive motor, verified the coupling, cleaned the condenser and checked charge. Bowl back to granita in under two hours. Total: $120 plus $360 part plus 1.5 hours = $600.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="story-card">
        <h3>Santa Monica, Donper XC212 margarita machine, event rental, wedding morning</h3>
        <p>Rental operator, machine leaking product from the front and margaritas coming out slushy-thin for a noon wedding. Diagnosed: front seal failed and scraper blades worn, so the cylinder wasn't scraping clean. Replaced the seal kit and scraper blades, sanitized, and ran a test batch to consistency. Turned around same morning. Total: $120 plus $240 parts plus 1 hour = $480. Operator added the machine to a pre-season seal-and-blade service.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

